<p>8-BIT NYC is a pixel map of what is happening in New York City today. It is built to be quick: open it, glance at the map and see what general neighborhood each event is in, without scrolling through long lists or checking a dozen different apps.</p>

<h3>How it works</h3>
<p>Every pin is something happening today. The listings are pulled automatically, a few times a day, from public calendars, ticketing sites and venues' own pages. Tap a pin to see what it is and when it starts, with a link to the source for tickets and the full details. Tap TODAY to look ahead to tomorrow, and use the filters to narrow things down by category or source.</p>

<h3>A map, not a mailing address</h3>
<p>The map is meant to give you a feel for where things are happening, so think of each pin as a pointer to the neighborhood. Listings come from outside sources and can change, so check the event's own page for the exact address and time before you head out.</p>

<h3>Who we are</h3>
<p>8-BIT NYC is a small, free, for-fun project made in New York. Spot something wrong, or want your events on the map? <a href="#contact" data-modal="contact">Get in touch</a>.</p>
